From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:03:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/34] flashnext: prompt pipeline, overlap, keep frames and
 NVFP4 prompt attention, each behind its own flag

Mixed-round sizing tables, the prompt hooks carried to the --tp 2 follower, bf16 scatter, n-gram hints beside the
pass, the MTP head's prompt rows as a prompt pass, an MXFP8 lane tile, permuted code pairs, gathers and router work
off the pass's stream, routed experts dealt over the ranks, overlap of long prompts with decode rounds, fused NVFP4
prompt attention, several prompts in one pass, early and late keep frames, one-launch shared attention on quantized
caches, and a wall-time cap on a prompt fill visit.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- flashnext prompt-tile2: FP8 checks sample only the call's rows; the bench prints RESULT lines
- flashnext: chunked DeltaNet chain on mma.sync behind TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_CHUNKED
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_TABLE sizes mixed-round pieces by decoders
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_MIXED_TABLE_ROUND times the table's limit as the whole round
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROMPT_FRAME carries hooks.prompt to the --tp 2 follower
- flashnext: roll back a round's drafted windows together (TF_FLASHNEXT_KEEP_LANES)
- flashnext tests: flashnext-prompt-frame for TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROMPT_FRAME
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SCATTER_BF16 sends the peer's scattered rows as bf16
- flashnext tests: flashnext-sum-bench, and flashnext-roce at the configured cap
- flashnext tests: hc-fuse at 546 and 300 rows, hc-wide below TF_FLASHNEXT_HC2_MIN
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_WARM_BESIDE runs the next chunk's n-gram hints beside the pass
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_MTP_PROMPT runs the MTP head's prompt rows as a prompt pass
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_OVERLAP runs prompts under the threshold whole and rides long prompts' pressure-sized pieces
  on decode rounds
- flashnext: rank 1's mixed piece takes its alone pass's prompt hooks; flashnext-overlap feeds prompt passes and
  counts EXL3 window-score rounds
- flashnext: MXFP8 lane tile for prompt lane calls behind TF_FLASHNEXT_LANE_TILE
- flashnext: permuted code pairs in the two-stage prompt tile behind TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_MX_PERM
- flashnext: the read-out gather on the sums' stream behind the own rows' in projection behind
  TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_GATHER_AHEAD
- flashnext: routed experts dealt out over the ranks behind TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_EXPERT_STRIDE (tp_flags bit 21)
- contract: fn_ep_picks_strided's launch record (nvcc 13.4/13.5 -O3 --fmad=false: 14/13/13/17/17 registers on
  sm_80/86/89/120/121, fn_ep_picks reproduces its 10/10/10/14/14)
- flashnext-overlap: hold the mixed pieces to an alone reference without the bf16 scatter, and check the reference
  repeats itself
- flashnext-overlap: a two-rank alone pass splits its sums only under TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PROMPT_RELAXED, so the
  bf16-rounded pieces need it too
- flashnext: the index_rows exchange and the router gather off the pass's stream behind TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_INDEX_AHEAD
  and TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_ROUTE_AHEAD
- tests: flashnext-index-ahead's timing as a BENCH line
- flashnext-route-ahead: both halves timed against the one call, the split's cost a pass
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_YS_BF16, the chunked DeltaNet readouts to the gated norm as bf16
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_ATTN_KV4_LEAN, fused NVFP4 prompt attention that skips no-op softmax corrections
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_ATTN_KV4_SMEM, kv4 prompt attention sharing widened tiles across rows
- flashnext: several waiting prompts' pieces in one prompt pass behind TF_FLASHNEXT_PROMPT_MULTI (tp_flags bit 22)
- flashnext: TP_SEQ_KEEP and TP_FRAME_FIRST for per-request TP allocation stalls
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR_MIN_ROWS and TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PLE_PEER for sub-1536-row --tp 2 prompt passes
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_PLE_PEER crosses the rows after the pass joins its pending sums
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_KEEP_EARLY, a round's keep_many frame sent when rank 0 rolled back, not with the next
  verify
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_KEEP_LATE, pending DeltaNet rows on each rank's half heads at --tp 2
- test(flashnext): rank ktests name the engine's own chunk in the identity
- test(flashnext): flashnext-keep-late names the engine's own chunk in the identity
- flashnext ktests: keep-early and keep-late size their identity's chunk as the served engine does
- flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_ATTN_LANES_ANY, a shared round's attention in one launch on quantized caches and half heads
- test(flashnext): flashnext-lanes-any reports an engine chunk mismatch as EngineChunk
- test(flashnext): flashnext-link-bench times the --tp 2 link by the RoCE path and NCCL
- feat(lanes): cap a prompt fill visit by wall time and bill short bursts to the share

