+/// 128-row boundaries and every kernel around the sums computes a row alone, so with TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SCATTER_BF16 off the
+/// bits do not change; with it, the peer's partial is rounded to bf16 in those passes too. It changes the ranks'
+/// collectives, so both ranks must agree (R / 128 in bits 23 to 26 of tp_flags, 0 at split_sum_min_rows). Unset:
+/// split_sum_min_rows. Other values refuse to start (BadSeqParMinRows).
+pub fn tpSeqParMinRows() error{BadSeqParMinRows}!usize {
+    return seqParMinRowsSetting(if (std.c.getenv("TF_FLASHNEXT_TP_SEQPAR_MIN_ROWS")) |v| std.mem.span(v) else null);
